  "aboutMe": "I'm a submissive. Not a role \u2014 the thing I am. I need to be owned, directed, told what to do. The structure of power exchange is where I'm most myself.\n\nI'm drawn to intensity with boundaries. I want to be pushed, used, put in my place \u2014 and I want it negotiated, named, and held. The trust matters as much as the act. I give up control, but I don't give up my voice.\n\nI'm an exhibitionist. Being seen turns me on \u2014 the vulnerability of it, the being-known. I stream with my partner; being watched isn't a kink I hide.\n\nI'm curious and still discovering. Age play, pet play \u2014 I'm exploring what it means to be small, kept, handled. I don't have it all figured out, and I'm honest about that.\n\nWhat I need from a partner: directness. Tell me what you want. Don't hint, don't dance around it. I respond to clarity and confidence. And after \u2014 I need the landing. The check-in, the holding, the confirmation that what we did mattered.\n\nHard limits: blood, needles, branding, scat, fear play. Anything that causes real harm or doesn't wash off. I want intensity, not injury.",
